Description: file manager and graphical shell for Cinnamon (combined package: Extra Pane persistence, Backup actions, coloured folder names)
 Nemo is the official file manager for the Cinnamon desktop. It allows
 you to browse directories, preview files and launch applications
 associated with them, and it is also responsible for handling the
 icons on the desktop. It works on local and remote filesystems.
 .
 This package combines nemo, nemo-data, libnemo-extension1,
 libnemo-extension-dev, and gir1.2-nemo-3.0 into a single package.
 .
 Fix: "Extra Pane" (dual pane) toggle state is now persisted between
 sessions via the saved-split-view GSettings key, both on toggle and
 on session restore.
 .
 New: a "Backup" item is added to the file/folder context menu. It
 creates a timestamped copy named "<name>_YYYY-MM-DD_HH:MM:SS" of the
 selected item in its parent folder.
 .
 New: a "Backup as Archive" item creates a single compressed archive of
 the whole selection (zip, tar.gz, tar.xz, tar.zst or 7z; the format is
 set with the backup-archive-format preference). Progress is reported in
 the window status bar.
 .
 New: folder names in the list view are drawn in a theme-aware green (dark
 green on light themes, light green on dark themes) so that folders stand
 out from files.
